{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":19447,"ns":0,"title":"Group (mathematics)","extract":"In mathematics, a group is a set with an operation that combines any two elements of the set to produce a third element within the same set. The following conditions must hold: the operation is associative, it has an identity element, and every element of the set has an inverse element.","description":"Set with associative invertible operation","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}